1. Understand the official timer / TCP / UDP tutorials for Boost.Asio;
2. Be able to write ordinary function callbacks and member function callbacks using `std::bind`;
3. Be able to explain the blocking and return conditions of `io_context.run()`;
4. Be able to write asynchronous serial reading of data from a lower\-level device;
5. Be able to write a TCP client / server;
6. Be able to write a UDP sender / receiver / echo server;
7. Be able to encapsulate the Asio communication module into a class;
8. Be able to integrate the communication module into a ROS2 node, instead of writing a blocking infinite loop inside a ROS2 callback\.
